## Control Principle

The incident does not justify adding controls simply because they are available.

Each improvement should trace back to a condition that affected detection, attribution, containment, or recovery.

The highest-value changes improve correlation, context, least privilege, and shared-device accountability without preventing IT staff from performing legitimate administrative work.
